			<item>
				<title>Change default kernel</title>
				<link>http://localhost:1313/docs/user-guides/user-config/change-default-kernel/</link>
				<pubDate>Mon, 08 Jun 2026 16:58:36 -0700</pubDate>
				<guid>http://localhost:1313/docs/user-guides/user-config/change-default-kernel/</guid>
				<description>&lt;hr&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;alert alert-info d-flex&#34; role=&#34;alert&#34;&gt;&#xA;  &lt;div class=&#34;flex-shrink-1 alert-icon&#34;&gt;&#xA;  &#xA;  &lt;span class=&#34;material-icons size-20 me-2&#34;&gt;&#xA;  info&#xA;  &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;  &#xA;  &lt;div class=&#34;w-100&#34;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Note&lt;/strong&gt;: This guide is for systems using the default &lt;code&gt;systemd-boot&lt;/code&gt; UEFI boot manager in Endeavour OS.&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Your system can have multiple kernels (or versions) of Linux. The default kernel is usually set to the newest one, but can be adjusted to user preference.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;First, you need to identify and adjust the kernel &lt;code&gt;ids&lt;/code&gt; used in the &lt;code&gt;boot loader&lt;/code&gt; config file.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;hr&gt;&#xA;&lt;h3 id=&#34;find-the-kernel-id&#34;&gt;Find the kernel &lt;code&gt;id&lt;/code&gt; &lt;a href=&#34;#find-the-kernel-id&#34; class=&#34;anchor&#34; aria-hidden=&#34;true&#34;&gt;&lt;i class=&#34;material-icons align-middle&#34;&gt;link&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;nav&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&lt;div class=&#34;nav nav-tabs&#34; id=&#34;nav-tab&#34; role=&#34;tablist&#34;&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#xA;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#xA;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;a class=&#34;nav-link  active&#34;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;   id=&#34;dabcefTab&#34; data-bs-toggle=&#34;tab&#34; data-bs-target=&#34;#dabcef&#34;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;   type=&#34;button&#34; role=&#34;tab&#34; aria-controls=&#34;dabcef&#34; aria-selected=&#34;true&#34;&gt;Use `bootctl` to view kernel info&lt;/a&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#xA;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;a class=&#34;nav-link &#34;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;   id=&#34;aefcbdTab&#34; data-bs-toggle=&#34;tab&#34; data-bs-target=&#34;#aefcbd&#34;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;   type=&#34;button&#34; role=&#34;tab&#34; aria-controls=&#34;aefcbd&#34; aria-selected=&#34;true&#34;&gt;Use `cat` to view current default&lt;/a&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#xA;&#xA;&#x9;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;/nav&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;tab-content&#34; id=&#34;nav-tab-content&#34;&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&#x9;&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;tab-pane fade show active&#34; id=&#34;dabcef&#34; role=&#34;tabpanel&#34; aria-labelledby=&#34;nav-1&#34;&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&#x9;&lt;h4 id=&#34;find-kernel-id-with-bootctl&#34;&gt;Find kernel &lt;code&gt;id&lt;/code&gt; with &lt;code&gt;bootctl&lt;/code&gt; &lt;a href=&#34;#find-kernel-id-with-bootctl&#34; class=&#34;anchor&#34; aria-hidden=&#34;true&#34;&gt;&lt;i class=&#34;material-icons align-middle&#34;&gt;link&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;ol&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Change to the root user with &lt;code&gt;sudo -s&lt;/code&gt; and enter your password.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
			</item>
			<item>
				<title>Downgrade with eos-shifttime</title>
				<link>http://localhost:1313/docs/user-guides/user-config/downgrade-to-specific-date/</link>
				<pubDate>Wed, 13 May 2026 14:09:31 -0700</pubDate>
				<guid>http://localhost:1313/docs/user-guides/user-config/downgrade-to-specific-date/</guid>
				<description>&lt;hr&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;alert alert-warning d-flex&#34; role=&#34;alert&#34;&gt;&#xA;  &lt;div class=&#34;flex-shrink-1 alert-icon&#34;&gt;&#xA;  &#xA;  &lt;span class=&#34;material-icons size-20 me-2&#34;&gt;&#xA;  warning&#xA;  &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;  &#xA;  &lt;div class=&#34;w-100&#34;&gt;Using &lt;code&gt;eos-shifttime&lt;/code&gt; does not revert AUR packages. The downgrade only applies to official Arch packages from the archive repositories.&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The &lt;code&gt;eos-shifttime&lt;/code&gt; application can revert system packages to their state at a specified date.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;ol&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Open a terminal window and run &lt;code&gt;eos-shifttime&lt;/code&gt; with root permissions.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Select the date to revert to on the GUI window, then click &lt;strong&gt;Revert&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reboot&lt;/strong&gt; to apply the changes.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ol&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;  &#xA;&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;  &#xA;    &#xA;      &lt;img src=&#34;http://localhost:1313/images/eos-shifttime.png&#34; alt=&#34;A GUI window for the eos-shifttime tool displaying a monthly calendar. The selected date is January 2, 2026.&#34; width=&#34;652&#34; height=&#34;543&#34; loading=&#34;lazy&#34;&gt;&#xA;    &#xA;  &#xA;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
			</item>
			<item>
				<title>Install new theme in Typora</title>
				<link>http://localhost:1313/docs/user-guides/user-config/install-new-theme-in-typora/</link>
				<pubDate>Thu, 25 Jun 2026 10:37:17 -0700</pubDate>
				<guid>http://localhost:1313/docs/user-guides/user-config/install-new-theme-in-typora/</guid>
				<description>&lt;hr&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#xA;&lt;strong&gt;Typora&lt;/strong&gt; is a minimalist text editor that renders markdown and code in real-time. The software comes with several default themes that can be applied through the &lt;strong&gt;Themes&lt;/strong&gt; option menu.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;First, find which custom theme you&amp;rsquo;d like to install from the &lt;a href=&#34;https://theme.typora.io/&#34; rel=&#34;external&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34;&gt;Typora themes page&lt;svg width=&#34;16&#34; height=&#34;16&#34; viewBox=&#34;0 0 24 24&#34; xmlns=&#34;http://www.w3.org/2000/svg&#34;&gt;&lt;path fill=&#34;currentColor&#34; d=&#34;M14 5c-.552 0-1-.448-1-1s.448-1 1-1h6c.552 0 1 .448 1 1v6c0 .552-.448 1-1 1s-1-.448-1-1v-3.586l-7.293 7.293c-.391.39-1.024.39-1.414 0-.391-.391-.391-1.024 0-1.414l7.293-7.293h-3.586zm-9 2c-.552 0-1 .448-1 1v11c0 .552.448 1 1 1h11c.552 0 1-.448 1-1v-4.563c0-.552.448-1 1-1s1 .448 1 1v4.563c0 1.657-1.343 3-3 3h-11c-1.657 0-3-1.343-3-3v-11c0-1.657 1.343-3 3-3h4.563c.552 0 1 .448 1 1s-.448 1-1 1h-4.563z&#34;/&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
			</item>
